# Cache + SEO / AEO / GEO

Applies to `xingai.app`, `invest.xingai.app`, and `travel.xingai.app`.

> Cache for performance. Purge for freshness. SSR/SSG for discoverability. One HTML source for SEO, AEO, and GEO.

Correctness and freshness beat cache hit rate. A deviation needs a note in that repo's ADR or README.

## One HTML

Users, Googlebot, Bingbot, GPTBot, and PerplexityBot get the same core HTML. No cloaking and no AI-only URLs. Do not add `Vary: User-Agent`.

Indexable pages put these in the first server render: `title`, description, canonical, one H1, the answer, FAQ, internal links, and JSON-LD when the page has it. JSON-LD uses the same fields as the visible copy.

A client locale toggle is not an indexable language. Do not emit `hreflang` until that language has its own URL and is in the first HTML.

## Layers do not clear each other

Browser, Vercel CDN, Next `fetch` / ISR, API or worker cache, and the database are separate. A green deploy does not prove the HTML or the data cache changed.

Invalidate the URL, tag, or fetch key that changed. Do not wipe the whole site unless the change is global. `stale-while-revalidate` does not replace that purge.

Hashed `/_next/static/*` may use `public, max-age=31536000, immutable`. Never mark an unversioned URL immutable.

## Do not recode the generic TTL sheet

Measured 2026-10-05. These are the production facts. Do not "fix" them by pasting `s-maxage=600` or a 30–60s market API onto the apps.

| Site | HTML today | What to do |
|---|---|---|
| `xingai.app`, Travel evergreen pages | `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate` and Vercel CDN `HIT`. Static HTML changes when the production deployment alias moves. | Leave it. A 5–60 minute `s-maxage` only re-fetches unchanged HTML. |
| Invest public HTML | `private, no-cache, no-store` because the root layout reads request headers. | Fresher than a 1–5 minute CDN cache. Do not add `s-maxage` until each locale URL renders one stable HTML document. |

## Invest data

The worker writes the decision cache. FastAPI only reads it. Do not add a request-path quote or FRED fetch to make numbers look newer. Do not present a cached research snapshot as a live price. If the page shows a market-derived figure, show the as-of time from the cache.

## Travel data

City guides, compares, stories, and other published pages change on deploy. `/result` and `/trips` are this browser's session or local history: `noindex`, omitted from the sitemap, never a shared cache entry. Do not put live prices, hours, or availability into evergreen HTML.

A regenerated model answer is not a published article. Published pages follow the deploy cache. Regenerated answers stay short-lived.

## Discoverability

Sitemap lists current public URLs only. `robots.txt` is not access control. `llms.txt` matches the public pages. After a public HTML or sitemap change, request the production URL and check status, title, canonical, H1, and JSON-LD. Spoofing a bot User-Agent only checks that the HTML matches; it does not prove the page was indexed.
